scope: |
  SSC3-J4 redone: the fusion DECISION moves out of the per-instruction walk to the loop
  ENTRY, which is the defect the J4 series has already fixed three times (an immutable List
  re-read on a per-call or per-instruction path). `exec` returns to its original 101 bytes
  untouched, so a body with no pair pays nothing; a body with pairs walks `execFused` at one
  integer compare per instruction.

  WIDENED to v3/bench-ab.sh: it hardcodes the ON arm as the DEFAULT build, which stopped
  being true when this pass became opt-in. Adding `ON_ARGS` lets an opt-in pass be A/B'd
  without editing the harness per measurement — otherwise every future opt-in pass repeats
  the same local hack.
next: ON_ARGS in the harness, then measure
